{
  "id": "m04-zero-triples",
  "title": "Zero-Sum Triples",
  "source": {
    "name": "Original exercise inspired by the classic 3-sum counting problem"
  },
  "rating": 1500,
  "tags": [
    "complexity",
    "counting",
    "hashing"
  ],
  "statement": "Given `n` integers, count the triples of indices `i < j < k` such that `a_i + a_j + a_k = 0`. Equal values at different indices count as different triples.\n\n**Input.** First line: `n`. Second line: the `n` integers.\n\n**Output.** One integer, the number of triples.",
  "constraints": [
    "1 ≤ n ≤ 1500",
    "−1000 ≤ a_i ≤ 1000"
  ],
  "timeLimitMs": 2000,
  "hints": [
    "Three nested loops are O(n^3): about 5.6 * 10^8 triples for n = 1500, which is too slow in most languages and hopeless in Python.",
    "Fix the middle index j and loop over k > j. You need the number of earlier indices i < j with a_i = -(a_j + a_k). Can you look that up in O(1)?",
    "Values are small, so keep an array cnt indexed by value (shifted by 1000) holding how many elements before j have that value. Update it after finishing index j. The sum a_j + a_k lies in [-2000, 2000], so the needed value may fall outside [-1000, 1000]; check bounds."
  ],
  "editorial": "A cubic loop is `~n^3 / 6 = 5.6 * 10^8` iterations at `n = 1500`, too slow. Reduce one dimension with a lookup table: iterate `j` from left to right; for each `k > j` add `cnt[-(a_j + a_k)]`, where `cnt[v]` counts earlier elements (indices `< j`) with value `v`. After the inner loop, increment `cnt[a_j]`.\n\nBecause every triple is counted once, with `i < j < k` determined by its middle index, the total is exact. Time is `O(n^2)` (about `1.1 * 10^6` steps) and space `O(V)` for the value range. The answer can be `C(1500, 3) = 560,625,500`, so a 32-bit int is just large enough in Java/C++, but a 64-bit type is safer.",
  "complexity": {
    "time": "O(n^2)",
    "space": "O(n)"
  },
  "starter": {
    "python": "import sys\ndata = sys.stdin.read().split()\nn = int(data[0])\na = list(map(int, data[1:1 + n]))\n# count i<j<k with a[i]+a[j]+a[k] == 0 in O(n^2)\n",
    "javascript": "const n = Number(readLine());\nconst a = readLine().split(' ').map(Number);\n// O(n^2) with a count array indexed by value + 1000\n",
    "cpp": "#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\nint main() {\n    int n;\n    cin >> n;\n    vector<int> a(n);\n    for (auto &x : a) cin >> x;\n    // O(n^2) with a count array\n}\n",
    "java": "import java.util.*;\nimport java.io.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\n        StringTokenizer st = new StringTokenizer(new String(System.in.readAllBytes()));\n        int n = Integer.parseInt(st.nextToken());\n        int[] a = new int[n];\n        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) a[i] = Integer.parseInt(st.nextToken());\n        // O(n^2) with a count array\n    }\n}\n"
  },
  "solutions": {
    "python": "import sys\ndata = sys.stdin.read().split()\nn = int(data[0])\na = list(map(int, data[1:1 + n]))\nOFF = 1000\ncnt = [0] * (2 * OFF + 1)\nans = 0\nfor j in range(n):\n    aj = a[j]\n    for k in range(j + 1, n):\n        need = -(aj + a[k])\n        if -OFF <= need <= OFF:\n            ans += cnt[need + OFF]\n    cnt[aj + OFF] += 1\nprint(ans)\n",
    "javascript": "const n = Number(readLine());\nconst a = readLine().trim().split(/\\s+/).map(Number);\nconst OFF = 1000;\nconst cnt = new Int32Array(2 * OFF + 1);\nlet ans = 0;\nfor (let j = 0; j < n; j++) {\n  for (let k = j + 1; k < n; k++) {\n    const need = -(a[j] + a[k]);\n    if (need >= -OFF && need <= OFF) ans += cnt[need + OFF];\n  }\n  cnt[a[j] + OFF]++;\n}\nconsole.log(String(ans));\n",
    "cpp": "#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\nint main() {\n    int n;\n    cin >> n;\n    vector<int> a(n);\n    for (auto &x : a) cin >> x;\n    const int OFF = 1000;\n    vector<long long> cnt(2 * OFF + 1, 0);\n    long long ans = 0;\n    for (int j = 0; j < n; j++) {\n        for (int k = j + 1; k < n; k++) {\n            int need = -(a[j] + a[k]);\n            if (need >= -OFF && need <= OFF) ans += cnt[need + OFF];\n        }\n        cnt[a[j] + OFF]++;\n    }\n    cout << ans << endl;\n}\n",
    "java": "import java.util.*;\nimport java.io.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\n        StringTokenizer st = new StringTokenizer(new String(System.in.readAllBytes()));\n        int n = Integer.parseInt(st.nextToken());\n        int[] a = new int[n];\n        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) a[i] = Integer.parseInt(st.nextToken());\n        final int OFF = 1000;\n        long[] cnt = new long[2 * OFF + 1];\n        long ans = 0;\n        for (int j = 0; j < n; j++) {\n            for (int k = j + 1; k < n; k++) {\n                int need = -(a[j] + a[k]);\n                if (need >= -OFF && need <= OFF) ans += cnt[need + OFF];\n            }\n            cnt[a[j] + OFF]++;\n        }\n        System.out.println(ans);\n    }\n}\n"
  },
